WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.700
Do you plan to make a New Year's
resolution? Will you make more than one?

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.140
38% of Americans will make a resolution,
according to a new poll from Ipsos.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:19.560
Of that group, slightly more plan to make
multiple resolutions, instead of just one.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.880
In the Ipsos poll, of those who plan to
make resolutions, money matters — such as

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.410
saving more, buying a house, or paying off
debt — shared top billing with eating

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:33.120
healthier and being more active. Ranking
slightly lower was losing weight, though

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.920
getting in shape is consistently popular
in the polls. Helping Americans to keep

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.290
those promises, many will wear a Fitbit
or a SmartWatch. 19% in a new Gallup

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:48.600
poll say they currently own one, and 15%
have worn one in the past.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.600
How many people will keep their New Year's
resolutions? 80% in to 2018 YouGov poll

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.580
agreed that most people don't
stick to those resolutions.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:03.220
Whether you make a resolution or not,
AEI wishes you the best in the new year

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.180
and good luck keeping those resolutions.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.400
Have you made a New Year's resolution?

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.619
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:18.150
scholars to cover in 60 seconds and be
sure to LIKE and subscribe for more

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.860
research and videos from AEI.

